  "source": "half-lap-art-frame.scad",
  "notes": "Extended from the supplied Onshape FeatureScript; half-lap remains the default. Eleven corner constructions preserve the artwork opening and outside size: half-lap, plain miter, mitered half-lap, bridle, mitered bridle, exposed-spline miter, loose-tenon miter, dowelled square corner, dovetail-key miter, blind mortise-and-tenon, and through mortise-and-tenon. Relevant controls appear for each joint. Zero-valued joinery dimensions choose automatic sizes as described beside each input. Loose tenons use rectangular, square-corner mortises. Through tenons finish flush outside. Inserts are separate colored pieces; select One corner insert for an individual STL. Nominal fits have zero clearance; fit to test stock. Drawings, machining sheets, the complete PDF, and grouped cut list follow the selected construction. Dowel cut-list entries are square turning blanks; equivalent round stock can be purchased instead. Dimensions are inches; geometry and STL exports are millimetres. The rear rabbet starts at Z=0; clearance enlarges only the back pocket.",
